Visible controls are rendered by Compose Multiplatform 1.12.1 / Skiko 0.150.1 / Skia,
with Compose Material3 1.9.0 and kotlinx.serialization 1.9.0. These JetBrains / Android
Open Source Project components use Apache-2.0; Skia uses a BSD license. Their notices
and complete primary license texts are distributed in licenses/.

Noto Sans SC / Source Han Sans: SIL Open Font License 1.1, included in
Noto-Sans-SC-OFL.txt. The font is reused from the Android application's licensed asset.

music-metadata 12.2.0 and its bundled dependencies parse metadata in a Worker.
@js-joda/core 5.6.5 is used by Kotlin/Wasm interoperability. Their exact package
licenses and notices are included in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. esbuild 0.28.2 and
fake-indexeddb 6.2.5 are development dependencies, not application media services.

hls.js 1.7.3 (video-dev contributors), Apache License 2.0, provides browser HLS
transport and media recovery. It is loaded only when live playback is requested.
Its complete license and bundled source notices appear in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

Protocol mappings and public lyric matching policies are adapted from the Android
ArchiveTune source under GPL-3.0, with original authorship retained in source files.
No music, user account sessions, signing private keys or third-party media are
bundled with the browser application.

qrcode 1.5.4 (soldair and contributors), MIT, generates login symbol modules only.
The symbol is drawn by Compose/Skia with a four-module quiet zone. QR image or
challenge keys never enter persistent media storage or portable backups. Its
complete license and bundled dependency notices appear in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.
jsQR 1.4.0 (MIT) is used only for independent test decoding, not shipped to users.
